{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545148-ten-curseborne-reactions-from-a-long-world-of-darkness-fan","id":1545148,"title":"Ten Curseborne reactions from a long World of Darkness fan","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-01T13:24:17-07:00","id":1545148,"title":"Ten Curseborne reactions from a long World of Darkness fan","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2024/11/curseborne-reactions-from-longtime-wod.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2024/11/curseborne-reactions-from-longtime-wod.html\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2024/11/curseborne-reactions-from-longtime-wod.html\" target=\"_blank\"> https://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2024/11/curseborne-reactions-from-longtime-wod.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://draft.blogger.com/#\" target=\"_blank\"><div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"320\" height=\"180\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEhgCEz3h_rI6mLUO4KV43ZyC74_8y9hpVGtsvgK0CzQdfekaWpXI-LkVMGgYJWaDM6vw498Jb8Deh2D6EjrUz-TZGNaBzkO6k60ZUWMd0w0NsrhRKJIXdC0jkPykTy2pqooBohij6BQDl4J6muOBHmcJqpHVn1hm5saZEWojQA-J78vE5XvopoFG3p6Fc5i/s320/Curseborne.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEhgCEz3h_rI6mLUO4KV43ZyC74_8y9hpVGtsvgK0CzQdfekaWpXI-LkVMGgYJWaDM6vw498Jb8Deh2D6EjrUz-TZGNaBzkO6k60ZUWMd0w0NsrhRKJIXdC0jkPykTy2pqooBohij6BQDl4J6muOBHmcJqpHVn1hm5saZEWojQA-J78vE5XvopoFG3p6Fc5i/s320/Curseborne.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEhgCEz3h_rI6mLUO4KV43ZyC74_8y9hpVGtsvgK0CzQdfekaWpXI-LkVMGgYJWaDM6vw498Jb8Deh2D6EjrUz-TZGNaBzkO6k60ZUWMd0w0NsrhRKJIXdC0jkPykTy2pqooBohij6BQDl4J6muOBHmcJqpHVn1hm5saZEWojQA-J78vE5XvopoFG3p6Fc5i/s320/Curseborne.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Hey folks,<br /> <br /> I just finished my read through of Curseborne's manuscript and being the longtime fan(atic) of the World of Darkness I am, I thought I'd share ten thoughts as my initial reaction. Overall, I really like it and think that it'll probably be my World of Darkness/Chronicles of Darkness substitute even if it's very distinct.</b><br /> <br /> <b>1. It is a lot easier to run mixed groups</b><br /> <br /> One of the persistent struggles of World of Darkness was the fact that all of the gamelines might as well have been separate. Vampire: The Masquerade supplements were fairly useless for Werewolf players and the same for Mage ones. You could do crossover but it was strongly discouraged with everyone going, essentially, &quot;if it's not like us, kill it.&quot; This is not the case for Curseborne and all of the supernatural Lineages basically can get along even if they don't necessarily do. As such, this has a lot more potential for mixed groups of wizards, vampires, and werewolves.<br /> <br /> <b>2. It is a very weird world</b><br /> <br /> If I had to use video game references, I'd say Curseborne is far more Alan Wake and Control than it is Bloodlines. The world is full of inexplicable uncontrollable magical phenomenon that can't be explained but only dealt with. I'd argue it's more Doom Patrol than even Hellblazer. For the most simplistic example, in Bloodlines, you deal with a haunted hotel based on the Overlook from The Shining. It's haunted because it has a serial killer's ghost in it. In Curseborne, you may actually be dealing with the hotel itself being evil and actively working against you.<br /> <br /> <b>3. It is more Chronicles of Darkness than World of Darkness</b><br /> <br /> I feel like this description is almost cheating as its true but due to the other things listed here. However, it's something that should be stated upfront. Chronicles of Darkness was a horror game set in the &quot;real&quot; world with disorganized supernaturals wandering among us and weird phenomenon. World of Darkness was heavily organized conspiracies in a stylized Gothic Punk world. The fact Curseborne is way more the former than the latter shouldn't be expected since, well, OPP really developed the Chronicles of Darkness world in the first place.<br /> <br /> <b>4. Characters are antiheroes not monsters</b><br /> <br /> A big difference drawn starkly between the Accursed and the vampires of, say, 5th Edition is that the Accursed have some serious problems but aren't automatically required to flip out and kill everyone. They're significantly more able to keep their humanity (for whatever value that is) and are far more &quot;people with powers that have serious drawbacks&quot; versus &quot;alien in human suit&quot; as sometimes Werewolf and Changeling were. They aren't required to use their powers to help people but the gameworld doesn't imply a Blackhart who eats the addictions or withdrawal pain of addicts is Doing It WrongTM. The game also provides a bunch of truly alien beings to contrast against the more human-like PCs.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://draft.blogger.com/#\" target=\"_blank\"><img width=\"247\" height=\"320\" data-align=\"right\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEh63lYCjNdex_G6rl8AqCDvt0fKPcWxyOUg-dGGLmCowNu8rU1ZBzyL-VMhChtvUnQOLlS1mvj58l7eCFyBtZb5l9X8mH035oqmBbbxxy1l152U1Y8Zp0S2q59a2-2XeuyilACvV1QjBTbd2IXewhuTINEW5GHWgvqaSFmTp5zfxaI4wywijULLo3_Dulmf/s320/6363c8819ceb405440d6962cfa5e5056_original.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEh63lYCjNdex_G6rl8AqCDvt0fKPcWxyOUg-dGGLmCowNu8rU1ZBzyL-VMhChtvUnQOLlS1mvj58l7eCFyBtZb5l9X8mH035oqmBbbxxy1l152U1Y8Zp0S2q59a2-2XeuyilACvV1QjBTbd2IXewhuTINEW5GHWgvqaSFmTp5zfxaI4wywijULLo3_Dulmf/s320/6363c8819ceb405440d6962cfa5e5056_original.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEh63lYCjNdex_G6rl8AqCDvt0fKPcWxyOUg-dGGLmCowNu8rU1ZBzyL-VMhChtvUnQOLlS1mvj58l7eCFyBtZb5l9X8mH035oqmBbbxxy1l152U1Y8Zp0S2q59a2-2XeuyilACvV1QjBTbd2IXewhuTINEW5GHWgvqaSFmTp5zfxaI4wywijULLo3_Dulmf/s320/6363c8819ceb405440d6962cfa5e5056_original.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_right js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></a><b>5. It makes a delightful mockery of the Masquerade</b><br /> <br /> One of the revelations of the 21st century has been the fact that not only do people believe all of the utter insanity that a lot of the conspiracy theories are built upon (as in millions of people) but none of this actually matters in day to day life. Barbara Jones the soccer mom may well fully 100% believe in vampires controlling the world but this won't trigger a Second Inquisition because no one is going to pay for it.She probably wouldn't support it either since she'd rather not be taxed for it. After all, it'll probably be someone else's kids getting eaten. The Accursed may keep their activities secret so they get chopped up in a lab but if a guy goes on Youtube proclaiming he's a werewolf, well, is that video footage real or AI?<br /> <br /> <b>6. Street level versus International Conspiracy</b><br /> <br /> While I'm sure this will change with later supplements, the implications are that the Families are about the highest level of organization you get in this world and they're disorganized as fuck. There's no Camarilla or Technocracy here but you might have a local vampire mob or court of supernaturals tun by a literal god in human form. As such, I expect the adventure you'll run will be far more like, &quot;rescue girl from a kidnapper who feeds on fear&quot; or &quot;close up portal to Hell in basement&quot; versus &quot;ancient vampire rises in the East and wipes out your Clan.&quot; Ironically, this makes international play far easier as there's no massive nation states of supernaturals to deal with. Weirdness in Tokyo will not have much effect on weirdness in New York, unless it does.<br /> <br /> <b>7. The system is simple and functional</b><br /> <br /> I'm more of a lore man than a crunch man but the system is unified and flexible in a way that wasn't the case with the Storyteller system past 1st Edition. Curseborne aren't as complicated as each individual splat and while I have annoyingly specific questions like whether the Hungry have fangs or not, whether subjects remember being bitten, and so on, the general fact is they are mostly humans plus a certain number of traits unique to each Lineage. You can make a character in about thirty minutes fitting just about any type of supernatural and gameplay should be extremely fast. Combat may be a bit more deadly than I like but that fits with the vibe they're going for.<br /> <br /> <b>8. Supernaturals are far more varied </b><br /> <br /> One of the annoyances of the World of Darkness was trying to reconcile the mythology of all the world's vampires with the explicitly Judeao-Christian myth of Caine. Which is fine for some games but a non-starter for others. Here, the Lineages are explictily more, &quot;we're kind of like X but have a origin related to Z.&quot; It's also implied by groups like the Hydes that new ones can be created at any time and we're only scratching the tip of the iceberg. Indeed, the Antagonists section makes it clear there's just a lot of outright WEIRD shit out there that defies description. This is a game that would allow you to make a Lineage or Families about guys who become werekoalas or music eating vampires in an hour and play them.<br /> <br /> <b>9. Otherdimensional weirdness</b><br /> <br /> it should come as no surprise that the gameworld has a lot of Gnostic influences and ideas of other realities breaking into this one. It's always been a big feature of OPP's Chronicles of Darkness and some of their other games too. These worlds are portrayed as wholly alien and can mess up parts of the world in ways that turn them into miniature Silent Hills or Twin Peaks. I always liked Horizon Realms in Mage and the Penumbra in Werewolf so these can both be present.<br /> <br /> <b>10. This is a labor of love</b><br /> <br /> This is something I am going to end on as I believe it deserves to be mentioned. A lot of recent products from a certain company (not naming names) feel like they weren't done by longtime fans and devotees of the product. They feel very corporate. This is something that clearly is the result of people who have a decades-long love for urban fantasy/horror gaming and it shines through in every page. OPP probably didn't have the opportunity to pursue every idea they wanted when working in someone else's sandbox that they clearly have the chance to do so now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-01T14:45:13-07:00","id":1545158,"title":"","content":"I do have to disagree a bit with point 4, those damnation and torment really push the character towards monstrous action (Like the primal damnation is rough) while some families likes the Vorare or the Heirs eats hearts and souls as their favored meal, the fiction seems to imply that a lot of older accursed are perfectly fine with acting like monsters.<br /> <br /> That said i do like that fundamentally, nothing really <i>forces </i>the player to act this way, the characters are not the good guys by any stretch but it does looks like forming a crew with other player character and relying on their family can help an accursed hanging on to their humanity and there is not mechanical consequences for failing to do so, it makes the act of trying to minimize the harm your character might inflict all the more meaningful to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-01T15:17:33-07:00","id":1545160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545148-ten-curseborne-reactions-from-a-long-world-of-darkness-fan?p=1545158#post1545158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do have to disagree a bit with point 4, those damnation and torment really push the character towards monstrous action (Like the primal damnation is rough) while some families likes the Vorare or the Heirs eats hearts and souls as their favored meal, the fiction seems to imply that a lot of older accursed are perfectly fine with acting like monsters.<br /> <br /> That said i do like that fundamentally, nothing really <i>forces </i>the player to act this way, the characters are not the good guys by any stretch but it does looks like forming a crew with other player character and relying on their family can help an accursed hanging on to their humanity and there is not mechanical consequences for failing to do so, it makes the act of trying to minimize the harm your character might inflict all the more meaningful to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like the game is kinda trying to have its cake and eat it on the &quot;antihero vs monster&quot; thing. As you say some Families do just straight up eat people's hearts. The book makes repreated references to the Accursed being rebels against an unjust system but also to them being unapologetic monsters and at times it seems to conflate those two in ways that go to almost Beast the Primordial levels of hmmm.<br /> <br /> The Primal Damnation is a good example of this, you basically have to seriously injure or utterly humiliate somebody (and since there's no reliable mechanical way to humiliate people, you'll probably go for injury) but the book makes a point of saying they have to be able to &quot;fight back&quot;, which Izzy's narration kinda reglosses as &quot;have it coming&quot; so you do wind up being almost and edgy 90s superhero. Even the people who literally *eat people* apparently only do it to people who deserve it and yes that's from their PoV but the more neural narrative voice of the Adversaries chapter gets pretty judgy about which NPCs do and don't deserve to be victims too (check out the description of Street Crimilals vs White Collar Criminals).<br /> <br /> It's definitely one of the most 1990s White Wolf aspects of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-01T15:40:56-07:00","id":1545165,"title":"","content":"True, on the &quot;You don't HAVE to be a monster, you can be an antihero&quot; seems a better way of describing it.<br /> <br /> But I accent ANTI-Hero as any heroes you will be will be Angel, Nick Knight, Spawn, John Constantine, or the Punisher.<br /> <br /> I don't think you can be Peter Parker, Ocho.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-01T15:43:57-07:00","id":1545166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545148-ten-curseborne-reactions-from-a-long-world-of-darkness-fan?p=1545165#post1545165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think you can be Peter Parker, Ocho.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not intentionally, certainly, but it's actually pretty easy to make a character so never really needs to spend Curse Dice so you can avoid Damnation quite reliably.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-01T16:11:00-07:00","id":1545168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545148-ten-curseborne-reactions-from-a-long-world-of-darkness-fan#post1545148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Combat may be a bit more deadly than I like but that fits with the vibe they're going for.</div> </div> </div> </div>With apologies for double posting, this one confuses me.<br /> <br /> It is literally impossible for PCs to die in combat.<br /> <br /> It is at the very least *difficult* for any character to deal more than one point of damage with a single attack (and impossible to do more than two in most contexts), there is a positive, not negative, death spiral, and healing is extremely generous even ignoring the many options some splats get for healing even faster.<br /> <br /> How much less deadly could it *be*?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-01T16:17:44-07:00","id":1545169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545148-ten-curseborne-reactions-from-a-long-world-of-darkness-fan?p=1545168#post1545168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With apologies for double posting, this one confuses me.<br /> <br /> It is literally impossible for PCs to die in combat.<br /> <br /> It is at the very least *difficult* for any character to deal more than one point of damage with a single attack (and impossible to do more than two in most contexts), there is a positive, not negative, death spiral, and healing is extremely generous even ignoring the many options some splats get for healing even faster.<br /> <br /> How much less deadly could it *be*?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, maybe I read it wrong then and will have to give it a re-read. I took it very differently, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-01T16:22:32-07:00","id":1545170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545148-ten-curseborne-reactions-from-a-long-world-of-darkness-fan?p=1545160#post1545160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like the game is kinda trying to have its cake and eat it on the &quot;antihero vs monster&quot; thing. As you say some Families do just straight up eat people's hearts. The book makes repreated references to the Accursed being rebels against an unjust system but also to them being unapologetic monsters and at times it seems to conflate those two in ways that go to almost Beast the Primordial levels of hmmm.<br /> <br /> The Primal Damnation is a good example of this, you basically have to seriously injure or utterly humiliate somebody (and since there's no reliable mechanical way to humiliate people, you'll probably go for injury) but the book makes a point of saying they have to be able to &quot;fight back&quot;, which Izzy's narration kinda reglosses as &quot;have it coming&quot; so you do wind up being almost and edgy 90s superhero. Even the people who literally *eat people* apparently only do it to people who deserve it and yes that's from their PoV but the more neural narrative voice of the Adversaries chapter gets pretty judgy about which NPCs do and don't deserve to be victims too (check out the description of Street Crimilals vs White Collar Criminals).<br /> <br /> It's definitely one of the most 1990s White Wolf aspects of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not a big fan of some narrators but i do view all of them as unreliable, i think some families tries at least to offer justifications for their act while other simply do not care at all, the ZED and Faceless are good example of that in my opinion, they just straight up work in their niche and don't seem to try to moralize what they do much while other family reeaaally try to protect/help or put their curses to a good-ish use like the Premi\u00e8re or the Wardens.<br /> <br /> I will need to re-read the adversaries part of the book when i have a bit more time, but overall I'm getting the impression that most established accursed/family leaders don't give much of a crap about restrain and are generally given a pass as long as they don't put their family into hot waters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-01T16:25:45-07:00","id":1545171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545148-ten-curseborne-reactions-from-a-long-world-of-darkness-fan?p=1545170#post1545170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I will need to re-read the adversaries part of the book when i have a bit more time, but overall I'm getting the impression that most established accursed/family leaders don't give much of a crap about restrain and are generally given a pass as long as they don't put their family into hot waters.</div> </div> </div> </div>When it was 13 not 10 Points, I had it listed &quot;generational war&quot; and how the game takes from the WOD (or its own) that the oldest in the setting are absolute monsters the PCs are expected to oppose.<br /> <br /> There's not even a Camarilla-esque, &quot;take shit until you move up the Layer Cake.&quot; The book frames the eldest as eternal monsters who will always use lesser Accursed as cannon fodder and slaves.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-01T16:27:18-07:00","id":1545173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545148-ten-curseborne-reactions-from-a-long-world-of-darkness-fan?p=1545171#post1545171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When it was 13 not 10 Points, I had it listed &quot;generational war&quot; and how the game takes from the WOD (or its own) that the oldest in the setting are absolute monsters the PCs are expected to oppose.<br /> <br /> There's not even a Camarilla-esque, &quot;take shit until you move up the Layer Cake.&quot; The book frames the eldest as eternal monsters who will always use lesser Accursed as cannon fodder and slaves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah i think that's a big part of the Rebellion theme, your crew and you against family elders","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-01T16:40:10-07:00","id":1545175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545148-ten-curseborne-reactions-from-a-long-world-of-darkness-fan?p=1545169#post1545169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, maybe I read it wrong then and will have to give it a re-read. I took it very differently, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I might also have misread, but &quot;PCs can't die nonconsensually&quot; I've definitely seen mentioned by devs (although I have raised an errata that if that's the intent it needs to be made clear because right now it feels like they just forgot to say you die when you run out of hit points).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-01T16:42:38-07:00","id":1545176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545148-ten-curseborne-reactions-from-a-long-world-of-darkness-fan?p=1545170#post1545170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not a big fan of some narrators but i do view all of them as unreliable, i think some families tries at least to offer justifications for their act while other simply do not care at all, the ZED and Faceless are good example of that in my opinion, they just straight up work in their niche and don't seem to try to moralize what they do much while other family reeaaally try to protect/help or put their curses to a good-ish use like the Premi\u00e8re or the Wardens.<br /> <br /> I will need to re-read the adversaries part of the book when i have a bit more time, but overall I'm getting the impression that most established accursed/family leaders don't give much of a crap about restrain and are generally given a pass as long as they don't put their family into hot waters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think ironically I view the DGAF families more positively than the ones that say they're &quot;trying.&quot;<br /> <br /> Like the Wardens seem unambiguously to be a creepy cult that goes around ruining people's lives under the pretext of &quot;saving&quot; them in order to feed their hunger for desparation.<br /> <br /> (Incidentally stuff like this is exactly why I <b>hate</b> how much of this book is IC narration, literally opposite interpretations of the same bit of canon could be true depending on who you believe and it's actually unhelpful for running the game, it's even worse when it comes to things like Dead Urges and Hungry Feeding).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-03T19:01:15-08:00","id":1545273,"title":"","content":"The amount of IC narration and the angry, disillusioned tone of most of it actually remind me a lot more of the oWoD than Chronicles. It's not quite punk because there's no clear political direction to the anger. It's interesting, but most of the Chronicles games had a very clear premise and gameplay loop of what they expected the players to be doing, but Curseborne seems deliberately non-committal about the expected gameplay direction and the devs have reinforced this with a lot of &quot;do what fits your table&quot; messaging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-03T19:17:44-08:00","id":1545274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Niknokk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545148-ten-curseborne-reactions-from-a-long-world-of-darkness-fan?p=1545273#post1545273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The amount of IC narration and the angry, disillusioned tone of most of it actually remind me a lot more of the oWoD than Chronicles. It's not quite punk because there's no clear political direction to the anger. It's interesting, but most of the Chronicles games had a very clear premise and gameplay loop of what they expected the players to be doing, but Curseborne seems deliberately non-committal about the expected gameplay direction and the devs have reinforced this with a lot of &quot;do what fits your table&quot; messaging.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my original 13 points versus ten points, I had three more additional bits:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>There's generational struggle</b><br /> <br /> I mentioned the layer cake (Daniel Craig movie) above and how so much of the WoD lines are about working your way up the Traditions, Camarilla, and Garou Nation. Which isn't very punk. However, this game world seems to strongly indicate whatever Curseborne organizations exist are all shitty places to be and you're better going off on your own. The leadership are all immortal and enslaved to their Damnations so there's no reason for them to help you. It's more Anarchist than the WOD where everyone is a hypocrite and the system seems to be, &quot;just fucking do it yourself.<br /> <br /> Don't try to reform the system from the inside.&quot;<br /> <br /> 2. <b>It feels very Werewolf: The Forsaken meets Changeling</b><br /> <br /> Essentially, I get the impression that a &quot;typical&quot; campaign for Curseborne is territorial as territory comes up a huge amount in the game. You are Accursed who have your own spot of land in your local city and you need to keep it safe from whatever weird abominations and monsters try to force their way into your area. This is very much like old school changeling in that your'e constantly surrounded by weirdness versus being only occassionally bothered by it.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>The world is hostile</b><br /> <br /> The big argument the game makes is that curses are almost animist to the point that everything has something sticking to it to make the world worse. The world isn't any less or more hostile than our own but everything related to &quot;bad luck&quot; and nastiness in the world is either producing a curse or the result of one just hanging around. You could spend all of your semi-immortal life lifting curses and the results would be only better for everyone like curing SIDs, cancer, horrible car wrecks, and so on in an area. But it would be only a drop in the bucket to the world that is still spinning out curses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-03T20:27:02-08:00","id":1545275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545148-ten-curseborne-reactions-from-a-long-world-of-darkness-fan?p=1545274#post1545274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. <b>It feels very Werewolf: The Forsaken meets Changeling</b><br /> <br /> Essentially, I get the impression that a &quot;typical&quot; campaign for Curseborne is territorial as territory comes up a huge amount in the game. You are Accursed who have your own spot of land in your local city and you need to keep it safe from whatever weird abominations and monsters try to force their way into your area. This is very much like old school changeling in that your'e constantly surrounded by weirdness versus being only occassionally bothered by it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still chewing on my three big favorite things/three things I'd like to see worked on, and this doesn't land on either list, but it was a very weird occurence to find myself thinking this a lot while reading, so I'm glad someone said it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545148-ten-curseborne-reactions-from-a-long-world-of-darkness-fan?p=1545274#post1545274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 3. <b>The world is hostile</b><br /> <br /> The big argument the game makes is that curses are almost animist to the point that everything has something sticking to it to make the world worse. The world isn't any less or more hostile than our own but everything related to &quot;bad luck&quot; and nastiness in the world is either producing a curse or the result of one just hanging around. You could spend all of your semi-immortal life lifting curses and the results would be only better for everyone like curing SIDs, cancer, horrible car wrecks, and so on in an area. But it would be only a drop in the bucket to the world that is still spinning out curses.</div> </div> </div> </div>By contrast, the first item on my Like List is &quot;This World is Fucked, I Love It.&quot; The hostility that comes with curses as the base metaphysics is just <i>instantly</i> playable in all number of ways, and it doesn't need much to get your character wanting to do something about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-03-2024, 11:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-04T02:55:00-08:00","id":1545296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Niknokk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545148-ten-curseborne-reactions-from-a-long-world-of-darkness-fan?p=1545273#post1545273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The amount of IC narration and the angry, disillusioned tone of most of it actually remind me a lot more of the oWoD than Chronicles. It's not quite punk because there's no clear political direction to the anger. It's interesting, but most of the Chronicles games had a very clear premise and gameplay loop of what they expected the players to be doing, but Curseborne seems deliberately non-committal about the expected gameplay direction and the devs have reinforced this with a lot of &quot;do what fits your table&quot; messaging.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I get very oWoD vibes from the time and not necessarily in a good way. Like there's a nostalgia factor but as you say it comes across as sort of generic anger with no real focus or theme. Like it talks a lot about how the Accursed are these rebels against an unjust system but doesn't really focus on what exactly they think is unjust about the system or for that matter what the system is.<br /> <br /> At least in vampire we knew what we were meant to be rebelling against.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-04T03:10:25-08:00","id":1545299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545148-ten-curseborne-reactions-from-a-long-world-of-darkness-fan?p=1545296#post1545296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah I get very oWoD vibes from the time and not necessarily in a good way. Like there's a nostalgia factor but as you say it comes across as sort of generic anger with no real focus or theme. Like it talks a lot about how the Accursed are these rebels against an unjust system but doesn't really focus on what exactly they think is unjust about the system or for that matter what the system is.<br /> <br /> <b>At least in vampire we knew what we were meant to be rebelling against.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, in vampire, Anarchs were rebelling against the System while very clearly being no better. Juggler vs. Modius.<br /> <br /> I get the impression the way Curseborne is supposed to work is that the Families are the system and they're not working because Silent Hill/The Black Lodge/Archons and so on are leaking into reality worse and worse.<br /> <br /> But you can form your own individual family/crew.<br /> <br /> You are the &quot;fix&quot; basically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-04T03:38:41-08:00","id":1545302,"title":"","content":"I agree that the Anarchs were in many ways as bad as the Camarilla, but that's sort of my point. You could look at what the Camarilla was like and you could look at what the Anarchs were like and point at specific differences and similarities. <br /> <br /> You don't really get that with the Families because none of them really even resemble each other and you aren't even all assumed to bring to the same one so what you're rebelling against is much more nebulous. <br /> <br /> I think your point about how bad stuff is leading into reality more and more and this is the dysfunction you're meant to be rebelling against kind of highlights the issue. <br /> <br /> Accursed aren't Uratha. They don't have a sacred duty to preserve the borders of reality. If the Outside is leading into the world more and more there's no particular indication that this is the Families' job to fix or even that they would be capable of fixing it.<br /> <br /> It's hard to have a game about how the system isn't working when there isn't really a system to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-04T06:55:26-08:00","id":1545304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545148-ten-curseborne-reactions-from-a-long-world-of-darkness-fan?p=1545302#post1545302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's hard to have a game about how the system isn't working when there isn't really a system to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a nutshell - <b>Curseborne</b> do not have ANY gameplay loop, from my reading of system. Even <b>Vampire the Requiem</b> got 'we try to take over the city AND go down and down humanity spiral'.<br /> <br /> ( Generally agreeing with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28625\" data-vbnamecard=\"28625\">Nobody Special</a> points risen here. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-04-2024, 09:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-04T07:14:40-08:00","id":1545307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545148-ten-curseborne-reactions-from-a-long-world-of-darkness-fan?p=1545304#post1545304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In a nutshell - <b>Curseborne</b> do not have ANY gameplay loop, from my reading of system. Even <b>Vampire the Requiem</b> got 'we try to take over the city AND go down and down humanity spiral'.<br /> <br /> ( Generally agreeing with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28625\" data-vbnamecard=\"28625\">Nobody Special</a> points risen here. )</div> </div> </div> </div>To be clear, I don't have a *problem* with it not having a core gameplay loop (I actually prefer my games to be flexible in that regard), I just find it odd that it presents itself as if it's about things it doesn't feel much like it's necessarily about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-04T09:17:08-08:00","id":1545317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545148-ten-curseborne-reactions-from-a-long-world-of-darkness-fan?p=1545274#post1545274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In my original 13 points versus ten points, I had three more additional bits:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>There's generational struggle</b><br /> <br /> I mentioned the layer cake (Daniel Craig movie) above and how so much of the WoD lines are about working your way up the Traditions, Camarilla, and Garou Nation. Which isn't very punk. However, this game world seems to strongly indicate whatever Curseborne organizations exist are all shitty places to be and you're better going off on your own. The leadership are all immortal and enslaved to their Damnations so there's no reason for them to help you. It's more Anarchist than the WOD where everyone is a hypocrite and the system seems to be, &quot;just fucking do it yourself.<br /> <br /> Don't try to reform the system from the inside.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this actually highlights my long-term concern with the Rebellion theme in Curseborne.<br /> <br /> Remember that back in the day you *absolutely were not* expected to be working your way up in the Camarilla. The Camarilla was exactly how you've described the Families: shitty places to be and you're better off on your own. It was always meant to be a corrupt system you rebelled against. <br /> <br /> But there were systemic features built into Vampire that meant it didn't work that way. You were strongly encouraged to identify with your Clan, the focus shifted ever more to city politics and formal official structures and gradually &quot;work your way up in the sect&quot; became the default goal. <br /> <br /> Curseborne could easily go the same way. The mechanics strongly reward playing archetypal family members and while the Families are often framed as having bad elements it's also made very clear that it's not really viable to just not have one (Orphans exist but the implication is that being an Orphan is like being a Caitiff or an Autarkis, really bas with no real benefits). As we dig deeper into the lore and get the inevitable splatbooks it's likely that there will be ever more focus on what the Families are doing and what's happening inside them.<br /> <br /> I can very quickly see &quot;become my local family head&quot; becoming the default PC ambition, effectively replacing &quot;become Primogen&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-04T10:59:24-08:00","id":1545329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545148-ten-curseborne-reactions-from-a-long-world-of-darkness-fan?p=1545317#post1545317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this actually highlights my long-term concern with the Rebellion theme in Curseborne.<br /> <br /> Remember that back in the day you *absolutely were not* expected to be working your way up in the Camarilla. The Camarilla was exactly how you've described the Families: shitty places to be and you're better off on your own. It was always meant to be a corrupt system you rebelled against.<br /> <br /> But there were systemic features built into Vampire that meant it didn't work that way. You were strongly encouraged to identify with your Clan, the focus shifted ever more to city politics and formal official structures and gradually &quot;work your way up in the sect&quot; became the default goal.<br /> <br /> Curseborne could easily go the same way. The mechanics strongly reward playing archetypal family members and while the Families are often framed as having bad elements it's also made very clear that it's not really viable to just not have one (Orphans exist but the implication is that being an Orphan is like being a Caitiff or an Autarkis, really bas with no real benefits). As we dig deeper into the lore and get the inevitable splatbooks it's likely that there will be ever more focus on what the Families are doing and what's happening inside them.<br /> <br /> I can very quickly see &quot;become my local family head&quot; becoming the default PC ambition, effectively replacing &quot;become Primogen&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never got into Masquerade, but Requiem had a similar dynamic where the game's emphasis was much more on finding a place for yourself within vampire society rather than rebelling against it.<br /> And even if you did rebel against it you couldn't stop being a vampire anyway.<br /> Curseborne as it exists now doesn't have that dynamic just because it doesn't flesh out the Families very much and spends almost no time talking about how the Families and Lineages relate to each other outside the IC stereotype sections. So rebelling against Accursed &quot;society&quot; vs rising in it are both about the same amount of work, at least from the Storyguide's perspective of coming up with setting elements.<br /> It's hard to say where the community and the devs will take the game, though. Fingers crossed it can build up a new identity for itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-04T11:04:25-08:00","id":1545330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545148-ten-curseborne-reactions-from-a-long-world-of-darkness-fan?p=1545302#post1545302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Accursed aren't Uratha. They don't have a sacred duty to preserve the borders of reality. If the Outside is leading into the world more and more there's no particular indication that this is the Families' job to fix or even that they would be capable of fixing it.<br /> <br /> It's hard to have a game about how the system isn't working when there isn't really a system to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of have three arguments against most of the argument laid out, but for these two lines in general.<br /> <br /> 1. The Accursed may not have a sacred duty to preserve and improve reality to their own design like the Uratha, but the game is built on a Hopepunk Theme*, and in game this generally results in something easy to understand as a cross stitch of things that World and Chronicles did-the world is so obviously messed up because of these curses that a player character not benefitting from them is just going to motivated to do something about it <i>because</i> it's so messed up, and curses a) are not usually the sort of things that manifest maturally, there's usually someone responsible for them, and b) don't have a tradition of being presented as universally and eternally unfixable/unremovable, there's usually a way to solve that problem.<br /> <br /> Curseborne takes the angle that you don't need a sacred duty to do anything about the world, you just need to court Hope's two beautiful daughters-and there's a lot ot get angry at in the world of Curseborne, enough that you probably have something that pisses you off and you want to fix it, and now you have all this power from your damnation that, while not the same as courage, is a hell of a starting place for. It's a game that assumes you're going to do something because it's a game that prizes empathy and the actions taken under it's name, including revolution against the metaphysic.<br /> <br /> 2. Similarly, the system is present-blatantly so. The bigger problem is that it's vast, knotted, and not from any one singular source-and that last part might be where it's hard to engage with the game on these terms. It's a vast spiderweb of a lot of people who have made the world worse and have left their mark for having done so, even if not for any reasons we might appreciate or they might continue to care about. But that's why we return to the nature of curses and what makes it playable-<i>someone</i> did it, and usually there's <i>someway</i> to fix it.<br /> <br /> The Families are a microcosm of the spiderweb, wherein they offer resources and connections that do a lot to help you and support you, but are also clear nexuses where curses conglomerate and perpetuate, nevermind what the elder's do to benefit from their neck of the wood for their own ends. Players are actively encouraged to do something to radically change and fix the Families are representations of the larger problem.<br /> <br /> 3) There is admittedly a problem that comes with doing the corebook with the Exalted Essence model**, which is that it very neccesarily has to take a broad look at everything without having the actual, physical space of word count to get too particularly deep into much of it's subject matter-it's very much the shallow end of the swimming pool for Curseborne's world, as many first books in a line are of course, and honestly shallower still. THere's a lot of repeating themes and motifs and ideas across families, so if you're not quite sure what the problem with one Family is, you can look to their ideological neighbors and fill out the roster, but admittedly the book just doesn't have the room to go digging into each Family's blasphemous skeletons and blatantly harmful operations.<br /> <br /> But what the corebook can and has done is set out the terms for it's play, and it asks you to play in faith to that-there is something wrong with the Families, you can do something about it, and your characters should want to feel the need to do something about it. Curseborne's corebook doesn't need to specifically lay out things like the idea that the Eight Hands are a bunch of child traffickers/diddlers and that the Premiere want to flood the streaming service world with Honey Boo Boo knockoffs-it tells you there is a problem, and it lets your tables/chats figure out what that is and what you can do about it.<br /> <br /> It's more labor intensive for individual games, and as the Lineage sourcebooks (and possibly Family sourcebooks) come out and explores the lore of all of them, we're going to see people's games, under the lens of guesses about that lore, become right or wrong, but in the meantime, it is still plenty possible to explore Curseborne's ideas and take on systemic damages simply by virtue of explaining how the mechanics of those damages happen then leaving it to your imagination.<br /> <br /> Just because the system isn't laid out for your doesn't mean it isn't there-it means you have to uncover it before you can fix it, table by table, game by game. The dark mystery of Chronicles meets the Gothic rot of World, with a whole new malevolent (but solveable) delivery.<br /> <br /> *and boy howdy do I have thoughts on that.<br /> **BOY HOWDY do I have thoughts on that. I should say both of these don't treat them as negatives, but that they are the more problematic of everything done with the design choices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-04T12:15:20-08:00","id":1545334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545148-ten-curseborne-reactions-from-a-long-world-of-darkness-fan?p=1545317#post1545317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Remember that back in the day you *absolutely were not* expected to be working your way up in the Camarilla. The Camarilla was exactly how you've described the Families: shitty places to be and you're better off on your own. It was always meant to be a corrupt system you rebelled against.<br /> <br /> But there were systemic features built into Vampire that meant it didn't work that way. Y.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was, and is a way, still is, a major problem with how the wod games presented in matter of themes and what the games actually offered. <br /> <br /> As you said, vtm pushed you toward being a arch, but never fleshed them out and the entire system pushed you toward raising inside a sect. <br /> Ironically V5, while trying to bring back the anarch centric pov did the same mistake<br /> <br /> In wta, we're told the players, to save the world needs to escape the binding of the garou's society. But the whole gift system forces the players to obtain reputation by matching said society's reputation<br /> <br /> In mta, the theme present to you the idea that amges should strive for ascension, and to shape the world. But the game has constantly shyed away from ever presenting ascension as a viable goal. To the point that it is now basically a &quot;who knows&quot; issue. <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> I fear that with that repetition and the return to an annoying IC narration, that curseborne takes the wrong lessons from the WOD <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-04T12:30:11-08:00","id":1545335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545148-ten-curseborne-reactions-from-a-long-world-of-darkness-fan?p=1545334#post1545334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In mta, the theme present to you the idea that amges should strive for ascension, and to shape the world. But the game has constantly shyed away from ever presenting ascension as a viable goal. To the point that it is now basically a &quot;who knows&quot; issue.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage: The Ascension did a massive course correction that is still controversial with Revised. OPP ran with it in their supplements of the Avatar Storm as a watershed moment.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Masters fighting a pointless war are dead so....why are we fighting?&quot;<br /> <br /> The technocracy went from evil to being good-ish, the Traditions went on to become more ecumenistic, and a whole third faction was made.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-04T13:11:09-08:00","id":1545337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545148-ten-curseborne-reactions-from-a-long-world-of-darkness-fan?p=1545335#post1545335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mage: The Ascension did a massive course correction that is still controversial with Revised. OPP ran with it in their supplements of the Avatar Storm as a watershed moment.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Masters fighting a pointless war are dead so....why are we fighting?&quot;<br /> <br /> The technocracy went from evil to being good-ish, the Traditions went on to become more ecumenistic, and a whole third faction was made.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's not just the ascension war. Even in M20 nothing pushes the players toward seeking ascension<br /> And very ironically, since writers constantly refused to &quot;codify ascension&quot;, the nephandi got it first in book of the fallen<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-04T13:40:34-08:00","id":1545340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545148-ten-curseborne-reactions-from-a-long-world-of-darkness-fan?p=1545330#post1545330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of have three arguments against most of the argument laid out, but for these two lines in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not going to quote your entire post because I think that'll get unwieldy.<br /> <br /> I think we *might* be talking slightly at cross purposes here.<br /> <br /> My core issue (and it isn't even an issue really, more of an observation) with the &quot;rebellion&quot; theme of Curseborne is that it has sort of a generic (as one poster put it) &quot;angry, disillusioned&quot; tone without it being particularly specific about what your characters are angry *at*; you're just sort of assumed to be angry on general principles.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying there won't be specific things to be angry about in individual games, at individual tables, or revealed in individual upcoming sourcebooks, but that's not exactly a USP for an RPG. Outside of extremely experimental indie RPGs &quot;something is wrong in your immediate vicinity, you have the resources to try and fix it so you do&quot; is basically what an RPG *is*.<br /> <br /> The reason I said &quot;Accursed aren't Uratha&quot; is that CTPhipps seemed to suggest that the increasing incursions of the Outside, the proliferation of Liminalities and the general amount of occult weirdness in the world is what you're &quot;rebelling&quot; against, and that the fact that this stuff exists at all is somehow evidence that the system of Families isn't working. But that only makes sense (to me) if either the Families were causing all that stuff (which as far as I can tell they aren't) or if it was actually their job to stop it (which it isn't especially).<br /> <br /> I do get that in a broad sense &quot;the system&quot; is the metaphysical injustice of the cosmos itself but, again, that cycles back to the whole &quot;nonspecific rebellion&quot; issue. If &quot;the system&quot; is &quot;the entire metaphysical setup&quot; then you're not really rebelling against any specific problem, you're just kind of rebelling against the abstract concept of injustice, which feels almost like a pastiche of teenage rebellion.<br /> <br /> You can say that the Families are somehow a microcosm of this and...I suppose sort of insofar as they're composed of Accursed people and they spread curses (although often they spread curses hereditarily and a fair few seem to less spread curses than to be a mutual support group for people who find themselves Accursed in particular ways). But ultimately they're a microcosm in the same way that an actual family is a microcosm of society, it's still a bit pointless to get angry at your dad over broad societal ills he can't actually affect and may be just as bummed about as you are.<br /> <br /> Of course there is the fact that apparently every family is ruled over by out-of-touch exploitative immortals but that's, as far as I can tell something that at least partly only comes out in developer chats not something that's explicit in the book (certainly most family writeups don't include &quot;also we're ruled by immortal assholes&quot;). Plus it also, for me, defeats the purpose of having a diverse range of Families. Like why present 31 distinct groups of supernatural beings if they're apparently all going to be the Camarilla?<br /> <br /> (Edit) I think the other thing about the system you're rebelling against being &quot;the Accursed nature of reality&quot; is that you get right back to the original Vampire issue where the thing you're supposed to be rebelling against is the thing that gives you all the cool powers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *and boy howdy do I have thoughts on that.<br /> **BOY HOWDY do I have thoughts on that. I should say both of these don't treat them as negatives, but that they are the more problematic of everything done with the design choices. </div> </div> </div>I'd be interested in hearing both of these, especially your thoughts on &quot;HopePunk&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28625,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","user":"Nobody Special","date":". 11-04-2024, 04:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-04T14:19:04-08:00","id":1545341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545148-ten-curseborne-reactions-from-a-long-world-of-darkness-fan?p=1545340#post1545340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd be interested in hearing both of these, especially your thoughts on &quot;HopePunk&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The short version on hopepunk itself is I am a crusty bitch who thinks that's a non-sequitor or at least a case of missing of the point, in a rare case for a curmudgeon who spends most of her time pointing out words don't actually mean anything.<br /> <br /> THe longer version, where I use that word as a launching point for one of the things I see setting up problems down the line, is definitely going to take some explanation.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-04T14:28:18-08:00","id":1545342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545148-ten-curseborne-reactions-from-a-long-world-of-darkness-fan?p=1545341#post1545341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The short version on hopepunk itself is I am a crusty bitch who thinks that's a non-sequitor or at least a case of missing of the point, in a rare case for a curmudgeon who spends most of her time pointing out words don't actually mean anything.<br /> <br /> THe longer version, where I use that word as a launching point for one of the things I see setting up problems down the line, is definitely going to take some explanation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. <br /> <br /> FWIW &quot;setting up problems down the line&quot; is very much my concern with the rebellion theme. I just can't see Families not ultimately working out the same way as every other splat in every other game; people mostly playing to type and largely on the same side as their splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-04T14:32:41-08:00","id":1545343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545148-ten-curseborne-reactions-from-a-long-world-of-darkness-fan?p=1545341#post1545341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The short version on hopepunk itself is I am a crusty bitch who thinks that's a non-sequitor or at least a case of missing of the point, in a rare case for a curmudgeon who spends most of her time pointing out words don't actually mean anything.<br /> <br /> THe longer version, where I use that word as a launching point for one of the things I see setting up problems down the line, is definitely going to take some explanation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think HopePunk is merely meant to be punk without the nihilism.<br /> <br /> &quot;The system is fucked, awful, and abusive but maybe we can build something better.&quot;<br /> <br /> Versus classic punk<br /> <br /> &quot;The system is fucked, awful, and abusive so let's get high.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-04T15:09:24-08:00","id":1545344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545148-ten-curseborne-reactions-from-a-long-world-of-darkness-fan?p=1545340#post1545340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not going to quote your entire post because I think that'll get unwieldy.<br /> <br /> I think we *might* be talking slightly at cross purposes here.<br /> <br /> My core issue (and it isn't even an issue really, more of an observation) with the &quot;rebellion&quot; theme of Curseborne is that it has sort of a generic (as one poster put it) &quot;angry, disillusioned&quot; tone without it being particularly specific about what your characters are angry *at*; you're just sort of assumed to be angry on general principles.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying there won't be specific things to be angry about in individual games, at individual tables, or revealed in individual upcoming sourcebooks, but that's not exactly a USP for an RPG. Outside of extremely experimental indie RPGs &quot;something is wrong in your immediate vicinity, you have the resources to try and fix it so you do&quot; is basically what an RPG *is*.<br /> <br /> The reason I said &quot;Accursed aren't Uratha&quot; is that CTPhipps seemed to suggest that the increasing incursions of the Outside, the proliferation of Liminalities and the general amount of occult weirdness in the world is what you're &quot;rebelling&quot; against, and that the fact that this stuff exists at all is somehow evidence that the system of Families isn't working. But that only makes sense (to me) if either the Families were causing all that stuff (which as far as I can tell they aren't) or if it was actually their job to stop it (which it isn't especially).<br /> <br /> I do get that in a broad sense &quot;the system&quot; is the metaphysical injustice of the cosmos itself but, again, that cycles back to the whole &quot;nonspecific rebellion&quot; issue. If &quot;the system&quot; is &quot;the entire metaphysical setup&quot; then you're not really rebelling against any specific problem, you're just kind of rebelling against the abstract concept of injustice, which feels almost like a pastiche of teenage rebellion.<br /> <br /> You can say that the Families are somehow a microcosm of this and...I suppose sort of insofar as they're composed of Accursed people and they spread curses (although often they spread curses hereditarily and a fair few seem to less spread curses than to be a mutual support group for people who find themselves Accursed in particular ways). But ultimately they're a microcosm in the same way that an actual family is a microcosm of society, it's still a bit pointless to get angry at your dad over broad societal ills he can't actually affect and may be just as bummed about as you are.<br /> <br /> Of course there is the fact that apparently every family is ruled over by out-of-touch exploitative immortals but that's, as far as I can tell something that at least partly only comes out in developer chats not something that's explicit in the book (certainly most family writeups don't include &quot;also we're ruled by immortal assholes&quot;). Plus it also, for me, defeats the purpose of having a diverse range of Families. Like why present 31 distinct groups of supernatural beings if they're apparently all going to be the Camarilla?<br /> <br /> (Edit) I think the other thing about the system you're rebelling against being &quot;the Accursed nature of reality&quot; is that you get right back to the original Vampire issue where the thing you're supposed to be rebelling against is the thing that gives you all the cool powers.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd be interested in hearing both of these, especially your thoughts on &quot;HopePunk&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is obviously just my interpretation of the book's setting and may be wholly wrong but my assumption is that the &quot;narrative loop&quot; of the Accursed is the fact that surviving in the world is actually quite difficult. It's not like Vampire: The Masquerade if you're one of the Hungry (where you're top of the food chain but for your rival bloodsuckers) or Werewolf: The Apocalypse (where you seek out evil) but more like Changeling: The Lost or a particularly fucked up version of the Dreaming. Basically, your very existence is something that is subject to issues of survival.<br /> <br /> Basically, Accursed are only going to encounter supernaturals every few months but these supernaturals are a persistent threat to them as well as the mortals around them. Curses flow throughout the place and are getting worse for the Accursed.<br /> <br /> You wander around a department store doing your daily shopping and OOPS, it's now full of mannequins who steal souls.<br /> <br /> You want to visit your girlfriend and then found out she's been replaced by one of the Fae's cuckoos. Why? Because it replaces the loved ones of Accursed.<br /> <br /> You find that a Battleground has opened up in your neighborhood and the war has come to your area.<br /> <br /> Basically, the world is incredibly hostile and you can either fight, flee, or die. You will eventually get drawn in either way, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-04T15:32:50-08:00","id":1545345,"title":"","content":"I think there's certainly an extent to which &quot;the world is inherently dangerous&quot; is a more baked in part of the setting and certainly &quot;just getting by as an accursed&quot; seems to be part of the deal. Then again it's not like being a neonate vampire was exactly safe.<br /> <br /> I'm also not totally convinced that a game can get by on a totally reactive gameplay loop; ideally you shouldn't *just* be trying to get by and reacting to whatever threat wanders your way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}